To generate a 20 kHz PWM signal with a 25% duty cycle on pin PA8 (TIM1 channel 1) with a 170 MHz system clock, we calculate the timer parameters as follows:
- Timer clock frequency ($f_{\text{TIM1}}$) = 170 MHz.
- Desired PWM frequency = 20 kHz.
- Choosing a prescaler $\text{PSC} = 0$, the timer counter clock is 170 MHz.
- The auto-reload register value $\text{ARR} = \frac{f_{\text{TIM1}}}{f_{\text{PWM}}} - 1 = \frac{170,000,000}{20,000} - 1 = 8500 - 1 = 8499$.
- For a 25% duty cycle, the capture/compare register value $\text{CCR1} = \frac{25}{100} \times (\text{ARR} + 1) = 0.25 \times 8500 = 2125$.

Here is the bare-metal C code using direct register access via ST's `stm32g4xx.h` definitions:

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void tim1_pwm_init(void) {
    /* 1. Enable GPIOA clock and TIM1 clock */
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN;
    RCC->APB2ENR |= RCC_APB2ENR_TIM1EN;

    /* 2. Configure PA8 in Alternate Function mode (MODER8 = 10) and select AF6 (TIM1_CH1) */
    GPIOA->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE8);
    GPIOA->MODER |=  (GPIO_MODER_MODE8_1);  /* Alternate function mode */

    /* Clear and set AFRH8 for AF6 (TIM1_CH1) */
    GPIOA->AFR[1] &= ~(GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8);
    GPIOA->AFR[1] |=  (6U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos);

    /* 3. Set prescaler, auto-reload period, and duty cycle */
    TIM1->PSC = 0U;                      /* Prescaler = 0 -> timer clock = 170 MHz */
    TIM1->ARR = 8499U;                   /* PWM frequency = 170 MHz / (8499 + 1) = 20 kHz */
    TIM1->CCR1 = 2125U;                  /* 25% duty cycle: 2125 / 8500 */

    /* 4. Select PWM mode 1 (OC1M = 0110) and enable preload (OC1PE = 1) in CCMR1 */
    TIM1->CCMR1 &= ~(TIM_CCMR1_CC1S);     /* Channel configured as output */
    TIM1->CCMR1 &= ~(TIM_CCMR1_OC1M);
    TIM1->CCMR1 |=  (TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_1 | TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_2); /* PWM mode 1: 0110 */
    TIM1->CCMR1 |=  TIM_CCMR1_OC1PE;      /* Output compare 1 preload enable */

    /* 5. Enable capture/compare channel 1 output (CC1E = 1) and set Main Output Enable (MOE = 1) */
    TIM1->CCER |= TIM_CCER_CC1E;          /* OC1 active high by default (CC1P = 0) */
    TIM1->BDTR |= TIM_BDTR_MOE;           /* Main output enable for advanced timer */

    /* 6. Enable the counter (CEN = 1) */
    TIM1->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;
}
